{{- $tiers := list -}}
{{- range $tier, $_ := .subagent_tiers.pi -}}{{- if ne $tier "frontier" -}}{{- $tiers = append $tiers $tier -}}{{- end -}}{{- end -}}
Launch plain JavaScript in an isolated VM; returns a background workflow id immediately, then the script's return value as JSON. title names the run's row. Use subagent for one bounded task and parallel subagent launches for flat independent work; workflows for scripted dependencies, pipelines or structured aggregation. For dependent implementation/check/review or multi-source research needing reconciliation or validation, await dependencies and pass intermediate evidence to downstream children; return only their cited synthesis, coverage gaps and unresolved disagreement, not raw reports or logs. Ultracode is on if the <workflow> system-prompt section says so or the latest user prompt says ultracode. Launch is refused when off; management still works.

Manage with {action: "status", id?} to list runs or inspect one, {action: "result", id} to retrieve its outcome, or {action: "stop", id} to stop it. Only one workflow may be active at a time.

The script reaches only:
- agent(prompt, { agentType, tier?, schema?, label?, phase? }): resolves to the child's final text, or schema-validated value (JSON Schema); rejects on child failure. agentType comes from subagent's list. tier overrides its pin: {{ $tiers | join ", " }}; default is its own tier; frontier is refused. label titles its row; phase overrides phase(). model, effort and isolation are refused.
- phase(title): default heading for later agent() calls, not a dependency; use await.
- parallel([() => agent(...), ...]): runs the thunks concurrently; results in order, null where one failed.
- pipeline(items, ...stages): each item runs through stage(previous, item, index) on its own, with no barrier between stages; null where a stage failed.
- log(message): adds a line to the result, as console.log does.
- args: the call's args value.
A leading `export const meta = {...}` is ignored. Nothing else is reachable: no files, shell, network, timers or modules.

Notes:
{{- with get $sizes .workflow_size }}
- Keep a run under {{ . }} agents.
{{- end }}
- Plan mode admits read-only agents only.
- One writer per write scope: broker approval is not write isolation, so give concurrent writers disjoint files.
- One fleet row; Enter lists agents by phase. Root steering does not rewrite the script; steer named children via subagent controls. Root Escape/Ctrl+Enter interrupts the root, not the workflow; use stop to cancel it.
